    "H4": "What Causes Kidney Stones?",
    "H4P1": "Kidney stones form when minerals in the urine — such as calcium, oxalate, or uric acid — \nbecome too concentrated and crystallize. Over time, these crystals grow into stones.",
    "H4B1": "Types of Stones: ",
    "H4B2": "- Calcium Stones (most common)",
    "H4B3": "- Uric Acid Stones",
    "H4B4": "- Struvite Stones",
    "H4B5": "- Cystine Stones",
    "H4B6": "Symptoms of a Kidney Stone:",
    "H4B7": "- Sharp back or side pain",
    "H4B8": "- Pain radiating to lower abdomen or groin",
    "H4B9": "- Blood in urine ",
    "H4B10": "- Blood in urine ",
    "H4P2": "- Frequent urination ",
    "H5": "Diagnosis:",
    "H5P1": "- Urinalysis ",
    "H5P2": "- Renal Ultrasound \n",
    "H5P3": "- CT Scan",
    "H5P4": "",
    "H6": "How to Pass a Kidney Stone Naturally:",
    "H6P1": "1. Hydrate well (2–3L/day) ",
    "H6P2": "2. Use over‑the‑counter pain relief",
    "H6P3": "3. Alpha‑blocker medicines may help passage",
    "H6P4": "4. Procedures may be required for larger stones (Ureteroscopy, ESWL, PCNL)",
    "H7": "",
    "H7P1": "",
    "H7P2": "",
    "H7P3": "",
    "H7P4": "",
    "H8": "5 Tips to Prevent Kidney Stones: ",
    "H8P1": "1. Drink enough water — aim for 2–2.5L urine daily",
    "H8B1": "2. Eat calcium‑rich foods (yogurt, soy, beans)",
    "H8B2": "3. Lemon water — citrate helps prevent stones",
    "H8B3": "4. Reduce salt (limit to <2300mg/day)",
    "H8B4": "5. Cut down animal protein — moderate intake reduces risk",
